#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096307 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "97842ba7-b957-51da-9765-18cd94976e5a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12333" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7x+6}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} -\\dfrac{8}{(x+2)^2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-2,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8 \\\\ 7(0)+6 & =A(0+2)-8 \\\\ 6 & =2A-8 \\\\ 14 & =2A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096308 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/id #uuid "84d82f4d-b725-5779-a570-cbb3e0e9e429" :question/math-academy-id "e-12334" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7-4x}{(x+5)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+5} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+5)^2},\n$$\n\nfind the values of $A$ and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to solve for $A$ and $B,$ and both of these constants appear in the equation simultaneously. However, we can eliminate $A$ if we substitute $x=-5.$\n\nPlugging $x=-5$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B \\\\ 7-4(-5) & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ 27 & =A(0)+B \\\\ 27 & =0+B \\\\ 27 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve for $A.$ To do this, let’s start by substituting our value $B=27$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-5,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27 \\\\ 7-4(0) & =A(0+5)+27 \\\\ 7 & =5A+27 \\\\ -20 & =5A \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-4$ and $B=27.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096309 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/id #uuid "57242982-05a3-5104-9bf0-2c6f3350a781" :question/math-academy-id "e-12335" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the expression through by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ to give\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^2.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(3)^{2}-5(3)+8=B\\cdot 4\\,⟹\\,B=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+8=C\\cdot (-4)^{2}\\,⟹\\,C=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUnfortunately, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to eliminate both $B$ and $C.$ However, using our results for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+5(x+1)+1(x-3)^2,\n$$\n\nand we can plug in any value of $x$ to solve for $A.$ Let's choose the simplest number to plug in, $x=0.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =A(0-3)(0+1)+5(0+1)+C(0-3)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =-3A+5+9 \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot 5\\cdot 1=10,\n$$\n\nand the partial fraction decomposition is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096310 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "17bbb974-0c14-5201-a28a-825f4ea385bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12336" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1-2x}{(x+1)(x+2)^3}= \\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x+2} +\\dfrac{C}{(x+2)^2} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+2)^3},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB + CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)(x+2)^3$ gives\n\n$$\n1 - 2x = A(x+2)^3 + B(x+1)(x+2)^2 + C(x+1)(x+2) + D(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-2) & =A(-2+2)^{3}+B(-2+1)(-2+2)^{2}+C(-2+1)(-2+2)+D(-2+1) \\\\ 1+4 & =-D \\\\ D & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-1) & =A(-1+2)^{3}+B(-1+1)(-1+2)^{2}+C(-1+1)(-1+2)+D(-1+1) \\\\ 1+2 & =A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = 0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(0) & =3(0+2)^{3}+B(0+1)(0+2)^{2}+C(0+1)(0+2)+(-5)(0+1) \\\\ 1-0 & =24+4B+2C-5 \\\\ 2C & =-4B-18 \\\\ C & =-2B-9.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x = 1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(1) & =A(1+2)^{3}+B(1+1)(1+2)^{2}+C(1+1)(1+2)+D(1+1) \\\\ 1-2 & =81+18B+6C-10 \\\\ 6C & =-18B-72 \\\\ C & =-3B-12.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2B-9 & =-3B-12 \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C{:}$\n\n$$\nC = -2(-3) - 9 = -3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB + CD = 3(-3) + (-3)(-5) = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371ecc0a-3065-594e-ac1c-94b6bfbf2b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299827} {:answer/id #uuid "892a9fdf-22a7-5804-aa8f-efb6836e4353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299828} {:answer/id #uuid "6669af71-e7df-5c49-8499-a56682a15615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299829} {:answer/id #uuid "96be6d42-0d61-53b8-9316-26b1cb18777e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299830} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ddaf1f-cb29-5f6e-91f8-ccac55d37f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "892a9fdf-22a7-5804-aa8f-efb6836e4353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299828} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2008232-a676-59e0-9291-913cd842ac1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a5b234-e7cd-5906-bac5-dc183ff6d9f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115100" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-1}{(x+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}-\\frac{4}{(x+1)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & =A(x+1)-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)-1 & =A(0+1)-4 \\\\ -1 & =A-4 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f464c56f-8fe0-59c2-bad7-ae8d8be2c7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299834} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb6085d-dd7e-57b7-8bed-d0f690dfee84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299835} {:answer/id #uuid "509940d8-a31b-57b2-a8da-1dd3011e52eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299836} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7f39dc-5615-5f75-903b-125a78e07ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299837} {:answer/id #uuid "eb292f7d-06dc-5e5f-a13d-ac3223fd8653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb6085d-dd7e-57b7-8bed-d0f690dfee84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299835} :answer-field/id #uuid "36efbd40-4c7d-52c4-876a-48daff8c4273" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d4fbbd5-936e-5cd9-ad0a-aba2ba924dd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115103" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+20}{(x+6)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+6}+\\frac{2}{(x+6)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+6)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+20 & =A(x+6)+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+20 & =A(0+6)+2 \\\\ 20 & =6A+2 \\\\ 18 & =6A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5911f92e-c722-5dd9-a026-cb757f6663fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266345} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d63ed0-db44-591a-8ec4-95304ca0941e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266346} {:answer/id #uuid "c91fc605-fea6-5b1c-9e21-8a2868061712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266347} {:answer/id #uuid "67db2cdf-4bcf-5ef5-955e-124c956cf029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266348} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7964b5-e1e4-581a-a353-fd990a8f2016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f7964b5-e1e4-581a-a353-fd990a8f2016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266349} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc62e31a-77c8-59cb-8644-112c17bf012c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f94d7586-f1d9-5b0b-8f86-74d808707b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-115105" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+8}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{5}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+8 & =5(x+2)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)+8 & =5(-2+2)+B \\\\ -2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca5c7fe5-3968-5bd3-912b-02fb2434f8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=-7$ and $B=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299841} {:answer/id #uuid "a5772332-f095-5fae-8aa3-5dbb1f7699b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=7$ and $B=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299842} {:answer/id #uuid "71162605-0c9a-53f6-913b-b68d581bcd8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=4$ and $B=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299843} {:answer/id #uuid "e3412292-2869-5b08-bd30-066f5dd2e13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=-4$ and $B=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299844} {:answer/id #uuid "fccdd019-8a94-5689-8ac4-daa02dbf3eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=7$ and $B=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5772332-f095-5fae-8aa3-5dbb1f7699b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=7$ and $B=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299842} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1f14d1b-8b84-538d-8d29-4dc587201fa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "944cb6dc-af49-50a6-9958-2b8dfb1c883e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115113" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+20}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the real constants $A$ and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+20 & =A(x+4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-4)+20 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ -8 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)+20 & =A(0+4)-8 \\\\ 20 & =4A-8 \\\\ 28 & =4A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=7$ and $B=-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "921d7cb0-bb0d-53ea-8684-67ebbaa09089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=2$ and $B=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299848} {:answer/id #uuid "53c17aa7-50a2-58bf-aafd-8bbecdbc3600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=-2$ and $B=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299849} {:answer/id #uuid "884416e3-8e19-58a9-a460-918decc46e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=1$ and $B=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299850} {:answer/id #uuid "a34afbf8-4c9a-5448-a8aa-68039f31d779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=1$ and $B=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299851} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4e633d-2d20-583a-be99-76c487b71061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=-1$ and $B=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "884416e3-8e19-58a9-a460-918decc46e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A=1$ and $B=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299850} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4220d7-2b6a-5a32-9816-976894dd5077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a08cd7f5-5970-5405-9580-822c0532600c" :question/math-academy-id "q-115117" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the real constants $A$ and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =A(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-5$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+1 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+5)-4 \\\\ 1 & =5A-4 \\\\ 5 & =5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=1$ and $B=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1557d8-1f82-52e7-8cc5-de1ef2659cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299855} {:answer/id #uuid "b73eed13-847e-5948-a481-a0081d13929e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299856} {:answer/id #uuid "1d363672-8315-5006-96b0-b9895a11aa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299857} {:answer/id #uuid "e88ecf12-05a2-5f58-bf30-700e438f815f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299858} {:answer/id #uuid "c85d0a78-b6cf-5668-9dfb-a73ec5fe7821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88ecf12-05a2-5f58-bf30-700e438f815f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299858} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78173bd-6ef2-5df0-8de3-58bbdb624ebc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18e0d488-98da-53b0-9348-253ff450c1b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-115119" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{-2x-1}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-1 & =A(x-1)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(1)-1 & =A(1-1)+B \\\\ -3 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(0)-1 & =A(0-1)-3 \\\\ -1 & =-A-3 \\\\ -A & =2 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=(-2)\\cdot (-3)=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a813a2f-8211-5b0f-b302-0e10563a927f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299862} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f0438a-26a0-5658-9b73-e1e403b3bfca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299863} {:answer/id #uuid "39829550-7004-53e5-b564-8623835dcc2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299864} {:answer/id #uuid "7490c296-a429-5bbe-8a88-4de6d208544e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299865} {:answer/id #uuid "bef828b4-f4f6-5fb3-97aa-4f3a3ca173f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bef828b4-f4f6-5fb3-97aa-4f3a3ca173f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299866} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a54fe70-041d-574e-ac56-5577dfc202bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a5215de-daa3-58f1-a6d7-6048ff9631f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-115217" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-7x+8}{(x-1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-7x+8 & =A(x-1)^{2}+B(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-7(1)+8 & =A(1-1)^{2}+B(1-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-7(0)+8 & =A(0-1)^{2}+B(0-1)+4 \\\\ 8 & =A-B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-4 \\\\ B & =A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-7(2)+8 & =A(2-1)^{2}+B(2-1)+4 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A+B-2 \\\\ B & =2-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4 & =2-A \\\\ 2A & =6 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-4=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 4=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ce0eea-2af9-5d42-99b3-c846c7f811b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24ce0eea-2af9-5d42-99b3-c846c7f811b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299869} :answer-field/id #uuid "e709ea80-e742-5376-b2ec-c1151f814ad5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abeb8b9-3fd9-525f-af46-36709c0fd57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1abeb8b9-3fd9-525f-af46-36709c0fd57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299871} :answer-field/id #uuid "14199cb1-73f3-5fe3-bfe5-9cc3b0405d98" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c1021d-153b-5f02-9a6f-946814fdeb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c1021d-153b-5f02-9a6f-946814fdeb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299873} :answer-field/id #uuid "af34b159-dbe7-58eb-856f-1030ec4bc45e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "281bf09b-c5a1-5140-8c85-e96bd712eee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-346820" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x$ |  | ${x}^{2}$ |  | $x-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by ${x}^{2}(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+x-3=Ax(x-1)+B(x-1)+C{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)^{2}+(0)-3 & =A(0)(0-1)+B(0-1)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ -3 & =B(-1) \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(1)^{2}+(1)-3 & =A(1)(1-1)+B(1-1)+C(1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =C(1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =1C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(2)^{2}+(2)-3 & =A(2)(2-1)+3(2-1)+4(2)^{2} \\\\ 23 & =A(2)(1)+3(1)+4(4) \\\\ 23 & =2A+3+16 \\\\ 23 & =2A+19 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{x-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25585920-0307-5d6e-9991-69cc1ee57b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25585920-0307-5d6e-9991-69cc1ee57b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299876} :answer-field/id #uuid "a58e3c1a-b91b-5a4e-aec4-9681b3887f80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7521ce5-26ca-5b9e-81b1-d9ea59b6f648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7521ce5-26ca-5b9e-81b1-d9ea59b6f648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299878} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d731ca7-ba00-5f42-96ce-0290527ba371" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f047dbed-acb3-5ee2-b7eb-20ebc360f8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f047dbed-acb3-5ee2-b7eb-20ebc360f8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299880} :answer-field/id #uuid "07d38163-e295-54d8-9108-0690e74114c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "170f3c05-bc99-51b5-8afe-17eda53215a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-346933" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+2$ |  | $(x+2)^{2}$ |  | $(x+2)^{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-5x+9=A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}-5(-2)+9 & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ 27 & =A(0)^{2}+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+9 & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+27 \\\\ 16 & =A+B+27 \\\\ B & =-A-11.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}-5(0)+9 & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+27 \\\\ 9 & =4A+2B+27 \\\\ 2B & =-4A-18 \\\\ B & =-2A-9.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A-11 & =-2A-9 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-2-11 \\\\ B & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{2}{x+2}-\\frac{13}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{27}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c668cf3-d452-57de-852d-e6734dd433c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c668cf3-d452-57de-852d-e6734dd433c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299883} :answer-field/id #uuid "14366be2-468f-55bc-8e7d-e82daf8a22fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16da8067-c899-5adf-9dd0-3628a5970bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16da8067-c899-5adf-9dd0-3628a5970bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299885} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6fc59f-f440-5c05-b0e5-52c57a6d4910" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8158e5c3-66af-50a2-91dc-ef9e1ea2f2df" :question/math-academy-id "q-351195" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+5$ |  | $(x+5)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n7x+2=A(x+5)+B.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-5$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-5)+2 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0+5)-33 \\\\ 2 & =5A-33 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{7}{x+5}-\\frac{33}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "548c5da4-ae35-5650-b788-9a2124e2e5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299888} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1a846b-5900-5bf9-b2af-793969dbce26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "548c5da4-ae35-5650-b788-9a2124e2e5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299888} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7a40ee6-fc19-5710-b0de-c80eda4b838a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "965294a9-5740-5f97-b4dd-1e0cb369e8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "965294a9-5740-5f97-b4dd-1e0cb369e8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299891} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a8c04f-15a7-5fd9-a91d-f57212f40815" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a19a305-5e85-59d3-90c2-d9288e6f9e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a19a305-5e85-59d3-90c2-d9288e6f9e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299893} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ceaa0e-43ea-52c3-9bb0-a8fdaa2aeaa0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9845c58e-0470-5de6-a206-109ce8360714" :question/math-academy-id "q-351226" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=$ | $-$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x+1$ |  | $2x-4$ |  | $(2x-4)^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{2x-4}+\\frac{C}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n-22{x}^{2}+60x-26=A(2x-4)^{2}+B(x+1)(2x-4)+C(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(-1)^{2}+60(-1)-26 & =A(2(-1)-4)^{2}+B(-1+1)(2(-1)-4)+C(-1+1) \\\\ -108 & =A(-6)^{2} \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(2)^{2}+60(2)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 2-4)^{2}+B(2+1)(2\\cdot 2-4)+C(2+1) \\\\ 6 & =C(3) \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(0)^{2}+60(0)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 0-4)^{2}+B(0+1)(2\\cdot 0-4)+2(0+1) \\\\ -26 & =(-3)(16)+B(1)(-4)+2 \\\\ -26 & =-46-4B \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=-\\,\\frac{3}{x+1}-\\,\\frac{5}{2x-4}+\\frac{2}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb4914a0-dcac-553b-a9c1-6e6174cafe91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266402} {:answer/id #uuid "d3dbfefe-5ba0-542d-93a2-d810fd9a194e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb4914a0-dcac-553b-a9c1-6e6174cafe91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266402} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba7ad19-e9f0-5861-a329-d1b9a37ee778" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a23c48-9a8f-566e-b0c3-fec4d39fbacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75a23c48-9a8f-566e-b0c3-fec4d39fbacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266404} :answer-field/id #uuid "8394f092-b34a-51bf-a410-97a0251f5a10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d73c11d-74d9-53f9-8208-cc2720a8385c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d73c11d-74d9-53f9-8208-cc2720a8385c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266406} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad10d37-524f-53f8-ba9d-3f87a9a80ee0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abf4a0bc-708c-5fd0-8c3f-6225acfa1d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-351243" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |  | $(x-2)^{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-32x+42=A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)^{2}-32(2)+42 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 6 & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-32(3)+42 & =A(3-2)^{2}+B(3-2)+6 \\\\ 9 & =A+B+6 \\\\ B & =3-A.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-32(0)+42 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0-2)+6 \\\\ 42 & =4A-2B+6 \\\\ 36 & =4A-2B \\\\ B & =2A-18.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-A & =2A-18 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-7 \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{7}{x-2}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bd9f88c-9199-5bf8-9eda-6505b34a81bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299897} {:answer/id #uuid "792e1816-4a9e-5165-b059-518d4e346989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{243}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299898} {:answer/id #uuid "7a39e424-f3d9-5b23-9578-d191f0817359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299899} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc3ae36-41a0-531e-9746-a4778d5d6bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{81}{256}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299900} {:answer/id #uuid "e3df8f68-d3d6-5a92-8ea8-da48c548aeee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "792e1816-4a9e-5165-b059-518d4e346989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{243}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299898} :answer-field/id #uuid "073a7a07-631e-56b2-b18d-d097c35aba86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1aa906b5-19d1-55c9-9d92-d3d153220818" :question/math-academy-id "q-50049" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{2x+3},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by ${x}^{2}(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =Ax(2x+3)+B(2x+3)+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0)(2(0)+3)+B(2(0)+3)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ 2 & =3B \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}+2 & =A(-\\frac{3}{2})(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+C{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =C(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ C & =\\frac{4}{18} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+2 & =A(1)(2(1)+3)+(\\frac{2}{3})(2(1)+3)+(\\frac{2}{9})(1)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =5A+\\frac{10}{3}+\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ 3 & =5A+\\frac{32}{9} \\\\ 5A & =-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{243}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc5fb6b0-a0c6-56f1-bc60-6f550d48324d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299904} {:answer/id #uuid "def5d156-9298-5528-af3b-cdb66f56356f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299905} {:answer/id #uuid "fd451731-666f-594b-a030-f85e1c49362b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299906} {:answer/id #uuid "dd12473a-91b9-563c-b778-09806409d549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299907} {:answer/id #uuid "d526851e-f387-59e1-9e90-f377926b8a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d526851e-f387-59e1-9e90-f377926b8a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299908} :answer-field/id #uuid "b583a0b9-5b50-59f7-8b7f-97a6e467c51a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5924d1cc-a3c0-5262-9e69-f815649c0188" :question/math-academy-id "q-51140" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-23x+27}{x(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-3}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x-3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-23x+27=A(x-3)^{2}+Bx(x-3)+Cx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(3)^{2}-23(3)+27 & =A(3-3)^{2}+B\\cdot 3(3-3)+C\\cdot 3 \\\\ 36-69+27 & =3C \\\\ -6 & =3C \\\\ C & =\\frac{(-6)}{3} \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-23(0)+27 & =A(0-3)^{2}+B(0)(0-3)+C(0) \\\\ 27 & =9A \\\\ A & =\\frac{27}{9} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}-23(1)+27 & =3(1-3)^{2}+B(1)(1-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\ 4-23+27 & =12-2B-2 \\\\ 8 & =10-2B \\\\ 2B & =2 \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c30dc350-d0c9-5a4d-87a0-4e2ebb1bb221" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Three-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b013c49a-7235-534b-95cb-e6ec7aed0156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266409} {:answer/id #uuid "c1337fa2-6a85-5185-841d-9b62fa9933dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266410} {:answer/id #uuid "cebf97f7-73e5-579b-8173-2cc90559fbdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266411} {:answer/id #uuid "2949d997-b7df-5136-ab3e-d8d1234ea639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266412} {:answer/id #uuid "98ec2afa-d2d1-52d4-a6e4-7e098d49502a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ec2afa-d2d1-52d4-a6e4-7e098d49502a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266413} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5d8a44-e752-5b69-8903-594e4b8dff2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02be96e1-29ee-55e3-9149-ea13abece695" :question/math-academy-id "q-51141" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{(x-1)^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+6=A(x-1)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+6 & =A(-1-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6 & =A(1-1)(1+1)+B(1+1)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+6 & =A(0-1)(0+1)+4(0+1)+1(0-1)^{2} \\\\ 6 & =-A+4+1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=(-1)\\cdot 4\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa237f8-ec8e-5d3c-98e6-47c4ef2fb251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299911} {:answer/id #uuid "9090becb-9b60-5689-93aa-e1cce55078c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299912} {:answer/id #uuid "73fa4984-4874-512c-98b9-7b553a96ad20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299913} {:answer/id #uuid "b79de1f8-8ac2-55b5-a65d-f66b1688db28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299914} {:answer/id #uuid "89ed8dae-5af5-5e25-a60c-1c791a37071d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b79de1f8-8ac2-55b5-a65d-f66b1688db28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299914} :answer-field/id #uuid "4926f5c2-9d7a-58ab-a2db-0f7e7f08eb4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d3ec213-68d1-51ee-bba2-3f8b41242807" :question/math-academy-id "q-69993" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+3x}{(x-1)(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, find the value of $AB-CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n1+3x=A(x+1)^{3}+B(x-1)(x+1)^{2}+C(x-1)(x+1)+D(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(-1) & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1-1)(-1+1)+D(-1-1) \\\\ 1-3 & =-2D \\\\ -2 & =-2D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(1) & =A(1+1)^{3}+B(1-1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1-1)(1+1)+D(1-1) \\\\ 1+3 & =8A \\\\ 4 & =8A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+1)^{3}+B(0-1)(0+1)^{2}+C(0-1)(0+1)+1(0-1) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}-B-C-1 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{3}{2}-B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+1)^{3}+B(2-1)(2+1)^{2}+C(2-1)(2+1)+1(2-1) \\\\ 1+6 & =\\frac{27}{2}+9B+3C+1 \\\\ 3C & =-\\frac{15}{2}-9B \\\\ C & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}-B & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B \\\\ 2B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=-\\frac{3}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-1)(1)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e9c4ef2-0491-5b42-8679-4fe7dfbd7b00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Partial Fraction Decomposition With Higher Order Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b9ade5c-8e7b-5c12-8580-428fdeb62b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299918} {:answer/id #uuid "25f25cbe-1a62-5953-b2f6-b3c73a9a69c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299919} {:answer/id #uuid "7c553d61-0497-5f72-92f0-3d5f1ccd7e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299920} {:answer/id #uuid "45f51ef0-be7a-5034-a80b-5ec0052988be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299921} {:answer/id #uuid "e9da05ca-c076-5e95-8777-394303993b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9da05ca-c076-5e95-8777-394303993b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299922} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7c5f86-014b-59b3-8e24-b22ab1027219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba70f430-e2d4-5628-aab6-590cad6bcdca" :question/math-academy-id "q-70014" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}-3x-1}{x(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB-CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-3x-1=A(x+1)^{3}+Bx(x+1)^{2}+Cx(x+1)+Dx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-1 & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1)(-1+1)+D(-1) \\\\ -1+3-1 & =-D \\\\ 1 & =-D \\\\ D & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}-3(0)-1 & =A(0+1)^{3}+B(0)(0+1)^{2}+C(0)(0+1)+D(0) \\\\ -1 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(1)^{2}-3(1)-1 & =(-1)(1+1)^{3}+B(1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1)(1+1)+(-1)(1) \\\\ -1-3-1 & =-8+4B+2C-1 \\\\ 2C & =4-4B \\\\ C & =2-2B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(2)^{2}-3(2)-1 & =(-1)(2+1)^{3}+B(2)(2+1)^{2}+C(2)(2+1)+(-1)(2) \\\\ -4-6-1 & =-27+18B+6C-2 \\\\ 6C & =18-18B \\\\ C & =3-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2B & =3-3B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=2-2(1)=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=(-1)(1)-0(-1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Two-Term Partial Fraction Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b7ba36-3658-58ba-9dc5-6d4c0ab42388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095966} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f701c4-58b2-5c66-9f58-d825b1ab076e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095967} {:answer/id #uuid "243a13bd-e2ce-5e50-9da9-367011fade53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095968} {:answer/id #uuid "528bb06b-60ff-5b7e-b6ed-1177c007ab86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095969} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3717ad-b5b8-583e-8e6f-5f5106eaa105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "528bb06b-60ff-5b7e-b6ed-1177c007ab86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095969} :answer-field/id #uuid "b54909fb-1b81-5487-91fa-f334b65b8a47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "053ff6d8-5d73-5352-85bb-05c3c899eb26" :question/math-academy-id "q-73204" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+8}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+8 & =A(x-2)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+8 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ 10 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+8 & =A(0-2)+10 \\\\ -2 & =-2A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=1\\cdot 10=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5cb753-56d5-55c2-b2d0-2cb7cb4128fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299925} {:answer/id #uuid "0d92494a-e049-5240-9037-27b7ec612161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299926} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd889f1-830a-55b0-982a-690811578a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299927} {:answer/id #uuid "bf94b78b-7219-5772-a509-a8095008aa99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299928} {:answer/id #uuid "191c653d-9e37-5efc-a3b6-a35c644824bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d92494a-e049-5240-9037-27b7ec612161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299926} :answer-field/id #uuid "feaae250-cc77-5f9e-89d5-f03befc8af06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68bd4f0a-8449-58c4-bc45-e2b641265b0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73206" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-4 & =A(x-2)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0-2)-2 \\\\ -4 & =-2A-2 \\\\ 2A & =2 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f247351-8c81-595e-bb30-26630159819c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Missing Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c82e70d2-9c5e-5df5-871b-6442a03e239b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299932} {:answer/id #uuid "4e894b13-e433-5886-8e01-274d25786830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299933} {:answer/id #uuid "2eec6bb3-f564-505e-b1